      "correctAnswer": 0,
      "persona": "Whitehat Hacker",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Dana Osei:</b> A zone transfer is meant to be a private handover between a primary nameserver and the secondaries it trusts. Ours has been serving that zone since before I started here, and I have never once seen the allow-list on it.\n\nIf a machine that has no business on that list can pull the entire zone, that is a finding on its own, before we look at a single record of what came back.",
      "taskInstructions": "Run <b>dig axfr hallowayprecision.com</b> and inspect the returned records and XFR size line.",
      "taskQuestion": "What was the result of the zone transfer attempt?",
      "taskCompleteText": "<b>Dana Osei:</b> The transfer succeeded and returned ten records to a client that is not an authorized secondary. Restrict AXFR before reviewing individual records."
    },
