      ],
      "correctAnswer": 0,
      "persona": "Blackhat Hacker",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Reyes Calloway:</b> A permissive zone transfer can disclose the current contents of a DNS zone in one request: hostnames, mail routing, and forgotten records still present today.",
      "taskInstructions": "Run <b>dig axfr hallowayprecision.com</b> and inspect the returned records and XFR size line.",
      "taskQuestion": "What was the result of the zone transfer attempt?",
      "taskCompleteText": "<b>Reyes Calloway:</b> The unauthorized transfer returned ten records. That is a complete current inventory of the zone, not its historical contents."
